# LeakSanitizer suppressions for third-party libraries only.
# libaccounts-glib keeps the contents of provider/service XML files it reads
# (g_file_get_contents inside the library) without freeing them.
leak:libaccounts-glib.so
# Qt 5 (qthread_unix.cpp): a QThread's QThreadData, allocated in the QThread
# constructor, is released by the thread's pthread TLS destructor. When the
# process exits right after QThread::wait() returned (QtTest's WatchDog at
# the end of qRun, QThreadPool threads at shutdown), that destructor may not
# have run yet, so LSan reports the 120-byte QThreadData under CPU load.
# Only allocations made inside QThread's constructor match; a QThread object
# leaked by netvfs code is allocated by that code and still reported.
leak:QThread::QThread
